From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:59:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: tear down an object the context refused by its id

A guest names each object it creates by an id of its own choosing, and the
context refuses an id it cannot take: 0, which names no object, or one that
another object already holds. It ends the context and leaves the object out of
its table. The creator has already made the object and tracks it in its
device, command pool or descriptor pool, which later removes every tracked
object from the table by id. An id another object holds finds that object, so
removing the refused one freed the original, which its owner still tracked,
and tearing the context down then walked a freed list entry. An id of 0 finds
nothing, so the refused object was never freed. Whichever owner removes the
original first, the table entry of that id is no longer the refused object's to
touch.

The object now carries the refusal: the table marks it when it turns the id
down, and its removal frees a marked object directly, without a look at the
table. An object the table holds is removed as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/venus/vkr_common.h  |  3 +++
 src/venus/vkr_context.h | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_common.h b/src/venus/vkr_common.h
index fd23df9d0eba15d3ab57ffd3ab77f4b3191da1d3..0b5fa20ae8b093f9db542134be5a346fdb7954ca 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_common.h
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_common.h
@@ -125,6 +125,9 @@ enum vkr_debug_flags {
 /* base class for all objects */
 struct vkr_object {
    VkObjectType type;
+
+   /* set when the context refused id: the object is not in its table */
+   bool id_refused;
    vkr_object_id id;
 
    union {
diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_context.h b/src/venus/vkr_context.h
index 3974ea49eb80c49884576576967e18ba822281fb..432ebbda29d271ddbca70208b25caa783b62ead1 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_context.h
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_context.h
@@ -252,12 +252,25 @@ vkr_context_add_object(struct vkr_context *ctx, struct vkr_object *obj)
    mtx_lock(&ctx->object_mutex);
    if (vkr_context_validate_object_id_locked(ctx, obj->id))
       _mesa_hash_table_insert(ctx->object_table, &obj->id, obj);
+   else
+      obj->id_refused = true;
    mtx_unlock(&ctx->object_mutex);
 }
 
 static inline void
 vkr_context_remove_object_locked(struct vkr_context *ctx, struct vkr_object *obj)
 {
+   /* An object whose id the table refused, because it is 0 or another object
+    * holds it, was never entered in the table, though its creator still tracks
+    * it and removes it with the rest.  Its id is not its own: it finds the
+    * other object, whose owner may have removed it already or still tracks it,
+    * or none.  It owns nothing but itself, so it is freed here, and the table
+    * entry of that id is left to the object that holds it. */
+   if (unlikely(obj->id_refused)) {
+      free(obj);
+      return;
+   }
+
    assert(_mesa_hash_table_search(ctx->object_table, &obj->id));
 
    struct hash_entry *entry = _mesa_hash_table_search(ctx->object_table, &obj->id);
